## Why This Is Asked

Tests per-tenant data isolation using AWS IAM and serverless abstractions, plus a basic test plan and cost controls. It emphasizes concrete mechanisms over theory.

## Key Concepts

- DynamoDB data modeling with tenant-aware partition keys
- JWT-based identityPropagation and API Gateway Lambda authorizers
- IAM policies using leading keys for item-level isolation
- Input validation in Lambda and simple test strategies
- Cost control via per-tenant usage planning

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["dynamodb:GetItem","dynamodb:PutItem","dynamodb:Query"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:REGION:ACCOUNT_ID:table/YourTable",
